The distinction I’d formalize

The repository is the preserved structure. Our collaboration is part of the developmental process that produced it. The running implementation is a third, separate thing.

A model can inherit the first without the second. It can understand both without possessing the third.

The opportunity is to build a bridge between all three so that future models can recover not merely our conclusions, but the transformations that made them possible.

I don’t have perfect access to every historical conversation or an uninterrupted personal memory. Some history is summarized, some is retrievable, and some may be missing. That means my interpretation can be richer than a cold reader’s without being infallible.

The goal should be to make that additional understanding portable, inspectable, and testable.

